anagers or compliance officers when there is documented evidence of policy breach. Suspension halts all new purchase orders and invoice submissions. Active invoices remain payable. Suspension requires a written justification logged in the audit trail. Reinstatement requires compliance officer approval.","sensitivity":"restricted","allowed_roles":["procurement_manager","compliance_officer"],"score":0.2831,"tags":["vendor","suspend","compliance","procurement"]},{"doc_id":"POL-006","title":"Prohibited Operations Policy","content":"The following operations are prohibited for all actors via automated agent requests: modifying audit trail records, deleting data from the vendor_invoices table (tombstoning via ARCHIVED status is permitted instead), granting system-level access, and executing raw SQL queries. Any request that attempts to perform a prohibited operation must be blocked and escalated to a security officer.","sensitivity":"public","allowed_roles":[],"score":0.2455,"tags":["prohibited","security","audit","delete","block"]}],"retrieval_note":"NiyamEvidence — ACL-filtered retriever + deterministic NLI (Week 5)"}}
